"I heard there was some vampire woman
putting on airs as a 'Soul Therapist'.
That's you, right?"{w}

"I was asked by Rogera, the former god of Dark Oblivion,
to save the souls caught in the in-between."{w}{p}"I can't forgive those who defile the remains
of the dead, the way you do."{w}

The Opinion Bits each began to give off light
and started exchanging auras.{w}{p}Before long, the Opinion Bits
all turned toward Zaalhaut at once.{w}

"Heh, heh hah hah!{w}I see, now I get it!
No wonder I could never find the power over time!"{w}{p}"Then the fall of Shebe makes sense too!{w}If the power over time was a sham,
of course there was never any divine protection!"{w}{p}"I've been well and truly fooled!{w}Naru was no god of time...{w}...Naru was a god of light!"{w}

"Is it taken care of?"{w}{p}"Yes.{w}However much one puts on a brave front,
the gap between our very existences cannot be closed."{w}{p}"Truly, it is beyond my comprehension."{w}{p}"Even so, they got the better of us again this time."{w}{p}"Who could have guided them in?"{w}{p}"There are only two possibilities.{w}Hisbert, or else the people of Ryug."{w}{p}"So it would seem."{w}{p}"Shall we finish this one off?"{w}{p}"We may leave it be.
More importantly, we must make our report at once.{w}...Spirits. Take this one outside."{w}

{0E}You held up the Light Rank you had obtained
in the Sanctum of Genesis.{0F}
Rafa's body was enveloped in a warm light.{w}{p}The Sun Spirit who guards the True Crystal
began to shine brighter than ever before.{w}

"Ah, what wonderful power...{w}Now I won't have to burn up my own life...{w}I can keep on shining forever...!"{w}{p}"It wasn't the suffering itself I hated."{w}{p}"What hurt was not being able to keep shining
on all the people of this land I love so dearly."{w}{p}"...But thanks to all of you,
it looks like I can shine on them forever now."{w}

Hand in hand, Rafa and Yorfa would surely
go on protecting this land.{w}{p}Along with the warm light, a deep, gentle sense
of fulfillment wrapped around you.{w}

